# Kite Weather
#
# Walking alone down a right-of-way beneath the power lines: wind across the
# open cut, the lines buzzing overhead and singing as you pass each pylon,
# the fizz of corona discharge, and chords far away.
#
# Chords only. No melody anywhere: every bit of expression lives in how the
# chords are played and shaped — filters that breathe open on each chord and
# snap shut, a pad that pumps against a groove it never hears, stabs whose
# velocity is their colour, dynamics that swell and drain by section.
#
# The harmony is one loop over a low E that never moves: E minor, F major
# over E, E minor, B-flat major over E — in tune, and pulling against the
# floor. The drums are a single bar built from Patina's own 909, destroyed
# (wavefolded, hard-clipped, 5-bit, ~8 kHz) and sliced into sixteen pads:
# the song plays it as recorded, chops and flips it, stutters it into rolls,
# and plays it backwards in the break. A tom tuned to E plays the chord tones.
#
#   bars 1-4    the pad alone, each chord swelling open
#   bars 5-12   the chopped break, the tuned toms, the pedal, off-beat stabs;
#               the pad pumps with the groove
#   bars 13-15  the break: reversed bars, a tom heartbeat, the pad closed
#               down to a resonant whine
#   bar 16      nothing but the wind, and a reversed swell rising through it
#   bars 17-24  everything, harder: wider filter swings, flipped chops, grit
#   bars 25-28  the drums go; the chords close down; the tritone is cut
#
# Build the samples first: python scripts/kite-weather-kit.py (renders/kite-kit/).
# 4/4 at 76 bpm; bar n starts at beat 4*(n-1).

bpm 76
gate 0.95
tail 4

automate tape_wow
0.05
automate tape_flutter
0.02
automate tape_age
0.35
automate tape_drive
0.35
automate chorus_mode
2
automate chorus_rate
0.4
automate chorus_depth
0.25
automate chorus_hiss
0.3
automate spring
0
automate reverb_wet
0.3
automate reverb_decay
0.82
automate reverb_tone
2800
automate width
1.15
automate comp_in
1
automate comp_threshold
-22
automate comp_ratio
1
automate comp_attack
3
automate comp_release
4
automate comp_makeup
2
automate comp_mix
0.5
automate fuzz
0
# the chorus is a send, not the bus: chords go through it, drums stay dry
automate chorus_mix
0
automate tape_drive
0.35 R:64 0.6:2@smooth R:30 0.35:8@smooth

# --- pad: Kaini, a saw and a saw an octave up (in tune, no detune)
track pad vel=0.55 patch=kaini chorus_send=0.6 reverb_send=0.3 duck=0.75 duck_release=0.32
([E3 B3 E4 G4]:4 [F3 A3 C4 E4]:4 [E3 G3 B3 E4]:4 [F3 Bb3 D4 F4]:4)x3
[E3 B3 E4 G4]:4 [F3 A3 C4 E4]:4 [E3 G3 B3 E4]:4
R:4
([E3 B3 E4 G4]:4 [F3 A3 C4 E4]:4 [E3 G3 B3 E4]:4 [F3 Bb3 D4 F4]:4)x3
automate pad.attack
0.4
automate pad.osc2_level
0.5
automate pad.osc2_pitch
12
automate pad.detune
0
automate pad.key_track
0.5
automate pad.filter_env
0
automate pad.resonance
0.7
automate pad.cutoff
260 700:3@exp 260:1@exp 850:3@exp 260:1@exp 1000:3@exp 260:1@exp 1150:3@exp 260:1@exp 1500:3@exp 320:1@exp 1500:3@exp 320:1@exp 1500:3@exp 320:1@exp 1500:3@exp 320:1@exp 1500:3@exp 320:1@exp 1500:3@exp 320:1@exp 1500:3@exp 320:1@exp 1500:3@exp 320:1@exp 420:3@exp 240:1@exp 420:3@exp 240:1@exp 420:3@exp 240:1@exp R:4 2600:3@exp 380:1@exp 2600:3@exp 380:1@exp 2600:3@exp 380:1@exp 2600:3@exp 380:1@exp 2600:3@exp 380:1@exp 2600:3@exp 380:1@exp 2600:3@exp 380:1@exp 2600:3@exp 380:1@exp 1300:3@exp 300:1@exp 1020:3@exp 300:1@exp 740:3@exp 300:1@exp 460:3@exp 300:1@exp
# closed down to a resonant whine in the break, open again for the return
automate pad.resonance
0.7 R:48 2.2:8@smooth R:4 0.8:4@smooth
automate pad.release
1.6 R:59.9 0.06:0.1@step R:3.9 1.6:0.1@step R:47.9 0.06:0.1@step
automate pad.gain
0.2 0.55:14@smooth R:34 0.42:4@smooth R:12 0.6:2@smooth R:30 0.4:14@smooth

# --- the pedal: Kaini, mono, a sub underneath; it never leaves E
track bass vel=0.6 patch=kaini gain=0.85 duck=0.35 duck_release=0.25
R:16 (E2:4)x11 R:4 (E2:4)x8 R:16
automate bass.mono
1
automate bass.sub
0.45
automate bass.attack
0.03
automate bass.release
0.5
automate bass.cutoff
380

